  keywords:
    - latex
    - format-conversion
    - scientific-documents
    - document-ai
    - reproducibility
  abstract: >-
    Deterministic cross-venue translation of scientific LaTeX documents
    (arXiv source to IEEE, ACM and Springer LNCS) through a Structured
    Intermediate Representation and per-class Jinja2 templates, with a
    four-gate verification methodology for content preservation.

references:
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      arXiv-MFT v3: a licence-verified corpus of 810 arXiv papers with
      all-three-format recompile status
    authors:
      - family-names: Pandey
        given-names: Adarsh
        email: engineer.adarshpandey@gmail.com
    repository-code: "https://github.com/CodeWithAdarsh007/paper-format-translator"
    url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24054291"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24054291
    version: 3.0.0
    date-released: 2026-11-08
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    keywords:
      - dataset
      - arxiv
      - latex
      - document-structure
    abstract: >-
      810 arXiv papers, each of which recompiled successfully into all three
      target venue classes, drawn from 1,533 licence-cleared candidates and
      1,419 downloaded source trees, with an 80/10/10 split by paper ID.
      Licence verification: 736 CC-BY-4.0, 60 CC-BY-SA-4.0, 14 CC0-1.0;
      810 of 810 on the allowlist, none off-list. Source LaTeX trees are not
      redistributed; papers are referenced by arXiv identifier.

  - type: report
    title: >-
      Paper Format Translator: format-preserving translation of scientific
      LaTeX documents through a structured intermediate representation
    authors:
      - family-names: Pandey
        given-names: Adarsh
        email: engineer.adarshpandey@gmail.com
    repository-code: "https://github.com/CodeWithAdarsh007/paper-format-translator"
    url: "https://github.com/CodeWithAdarsh007/paper-format-translator/blob/main/docs/report_final.md"
    year: 2026
    month: 11
    note: >-
      Undergraduate technical report, 1.0, consolidated 2026-11-08. Sections
      2 (Abstract), 5 (Introduction), 12 (Conclusion) and the Acknowledgments
      are published as first drafts and are to be rewritten by the author
